  "rationale": "The patient is experiencing feeding and eating disorders (poor appetite, forgetting to eat or drink, chewing and swallowing problems). The patient is in a moderate-to-severe stage and requires assistance with eating and drinking in an institutional setting. The primary immediate management goal is to directly increase food and energy intake and improve nutritional outcomes. The patient requires hands-on assistance with eating and drinking. However, staff or caregiver handfeeding assistance is not available at mealtimes."
